  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Privacy Intl 2021-2024 (2026) - Privacy Intl 2021-2024 - Ny strategi 2024</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Privacy Intl 2021-2024 (2026)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Privacy International (PI) is a London-based policy-research organisation established in 1990. PI engages in long-term efforts to advance the right to privacy locally and globally in collaboration with local partner organisations, aiming to contribute to increasing engagement in privacy issues by civil society and governments globally. 

During the pandemic, the right to privacy and issues of data protection have become even more decisive in the protection of human rights globally. Measures taken to fight Covid 19 have had serious consequences for human rights and tracing apps have been at the heart of debate globally. 

In its Strategic Plan for 2019-2022, PI has identified the following strategic areas:

- Challenging Corporate Data Exploitation
- Contesting Government Data and System Exploitation
- Defending Democracy and Dissent
- Safeguarding Peoples&apos; Dignity

PI has now applied for core support during 2021-2024 at a total amount of 22,3 MSEK

PI receives funding from several other donors, such as Luminate (core), Ford Foundation (core), OSF (core) as well as Oak Foundation, IDRC and Paul Hamlyn Foundation.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Privacy International (PI) &#xe4;r en Londonbaserad organisation med inriktning p&#xe5; policy och forskning som grundades 1990. PI engagerar sig i l&#xe5;ngsiktiga insatser f&#xf6;r att fr&#xe4;mja r&#xe4;tten till ett privatliv lokalt och globalt i samarbete med lokala partnerorganisationer, i syfte att bidra till att &#xf6;ka det civila samh&#xe4;llets och regeringars engagemang i fr&#xe5;gor om r&#xe4;tten till ett privatliv globalt. 

Under pandemin har r&#xe4;tten till integritet och fr&#xe5;gor om dataskydd blivit &#xe4;nnu mer avg&#xf6;rande f&#xf6;r skyddet av m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter globalt. &#xc5;tg&#xe4;rder som vidtagits f&#xf6;r att bek&#xe4;mpa Covid-19 har f&#xe5;tt allvarliga konsekvenser f&#xf6;r m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter och anv&#xe4;ndandet av sp&#xe5;rningsappar har debatterats globalt. 

I sin strategiska plan f&#xf6;r 2019&#x2013;2022 har PI identifierat f&#xf6;ljande strategiska omr&#xe5;den:
- Motverka f&#xf6;retags exploaterande av data
- Motverka regeringars insamlande och exploaterande av data
- F&#xf6;rsvara demokrati och olikt&#xe4;nkande
- Skydda m&#xe4;nniskors v&#xe4;rdighet

PI har nu ans&#xf6;kt om k&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;d under 2021-2024 till ett totalt belopp om 22,3 MSEK

PI f&#xe5;r finansiering fr&#xe5;n flera andra givare, s&#xe5;som Luminate (k&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;d), Ford Foundation (k&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;d), OSF (k&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;d) samt Oak Foundation, IDRC och Paul Hamlyn Foundation.</narrative>
  </description>
